# The OpenAPI specification this workspace generates its client from is published
# as an npm package, `@mmadel/openapi-spec`, to GitHub Packages rather than to the
# public registry. Only the `@mmadel` scope is redirected: everything else still
# comes from registry.npmjs.org.
#
# The scope is `@mmadel` and not `@epm` because GitHub Packages requires an npm
# package's scope to be the account that owns the repository publishing it.
# `epm-service` is owned by the user `mmadel`, so `@epm/openapi-spec` is rejected
# at publish time with a 400 and does not exist to install. (This is an npm rule;
# the Maven packages published from the same account are unaffected by it.)
@mmadel:registry=https://npm.pkg.github.com

# The token is READ FROM THE ENVIRONMENT and never written here. A token committed
# to a repository is a token to rotate.
#
# It needs `read:packages` and it must be a classic personal access token. A
# workflow's automatic GITHUB_TOKEN cannot be used: it reads only its own
# repository's packages, and the specification is published from `epm-service`.
# That mismatch surfaces as a 401 or a 404 on `npm ci`, never as something that
# says "token" - see scripts/check-packages-token.mjs, which fails first and does.
#
# Note that this line beats the same key in ~/.npmrc: a project's configuration
# wins over the user's. So the token goes in the environment, not in ~/.npmrc.
//npm.pkg.github.com/:_authToken=${NODE_AUTH_TOKEN}
